{%- doc -%}
  Outputs what a kit's contents cost bought separately, in the shop's minor
  currency unit.

  Source, in order of preference:
  1. `custom.kit_components` (list of nr_kit_component metaobjects): the price
     of each component's exact variant × its quantity (blank quantity = 1).
     If any component's variant can't be resolved, outputs 0 rather than a
     partial (too low) total.
  2. `custom.separate_components` (legacy list of products): the current price
     of each product's first available variant, one of each.
  Outputs 0 when neither is set, so callers can hide the comparison.

  This is deliberately NOT the kit's compare-at price: compare-at is shown by
  the theme as a previous price / sale, which a "bought separately" sum is not.

  Liquid can't return values from a snippet, so capture and convert:
    {% capture separate %}{% render 'nr-kit-separate-total', product: kit %}{% endcapture %}
    {% assign separate = separate | strip | plus: 0 %}

  @param {product} product - The kit product.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign total = 0
  assign components = product.metafields.custom.kit_components.value

  if components != blank
    assign incomplete = false
    for component in components
      assign component_variant = component.variant.value
      if component_variant == blank
        assign incomplete = true
        break
      endif
      assign component_quantity = component.quantity.value | default: 1
      assign line_total = component_variant.price | times: component_quantity
      assign total = total | plus: line_total
    endfor
    if incomplete
      assign total = 0
    endif
  else
    for component in product.metafields.custom.separate_components.value
      assign total = total | plus: component.selected_or_first_available_variant.price
    endfor
  endif

  echo total
-%}
